/* The input language reserves the terminal br for nondeterministic choice:
   br t1 t2 stands for the outputs of t1 and of t2, and a specification
   holds when it holds of both, although the automaton has no transition on
   br.  Main chooses between e and a e, both accepted from q0: sat.  The
   reduction marks its own branches with the same br, so a program's br is
   read exactly as the reduction's. */
%BEGING
Main x -> br e (a e).
%ENDG

%BEGINA
q0 a -> q0.
q0 e -> .
%ENDA

%BEGINT
Main : q0 -> q0.
%ENDT
